@kimmonismus They need highly purified/sanitized water to protect the electronics.

Water like that is on short supply.

Do try to be more genuine about your arguments, this line is very misleading

@kimmonismus The argument that ai consumes water is so funny, don't those ppl know how radiators and water cooling work. 
It's a fucking closed system where few water escapes. 
I have liquid cooling in my PC and I have filled it twice for the last four years.

@kimmonismus Data centers use water.

So do millions of factories making physical goods.

High usage doesn't equal high harm - per-task efficiency flips the whole AI water panic.

